{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>As the horns of a re'em to him.</b> To Israel — for he does not prey and devour like a lion, but pushes away with his horns like the re'em. For the intent was to drive out the nations and bring Israel into the land without killing the nations, as it says: תְּגָרֵשׁ גּוֹיִם וַתִּטָּעֶהָ (Psalms 80:9) — for He does not desire the death of the dead. And so the Sages, of blessed memory, said: 'Three letters Joshua sent: whoever wishes to flee, let him flee; whoever wishes to make peace, let him make peace; whoever wishes to make war, let him make war.' But they stiffened their necks to fight, and it became necessary to proscribe them. Accordingly, Israel did not make use of them at all as a lion makes use of its prey, but did to them as the re'em does to what it pushes away or overpowers — it does not eat it at all."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:56.970472483Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}